Cyber Defence Frameworks – SOC Report

Overview
This exercise introduced key cyber defence frameworks used by Security Operations Centers (SOCs) to detect, investigate, and respond to cyber threats.
Frameworks Covered

MITRE ATT&CK: Maps attacker tactics and techniques to improve threat detection and threat hunting.

Cyber Kill Chain: Breaks down the stages of an attack, helping defenders detect and stop threats early.

NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF): Provides five core functions Identify, Protect, Detect, Respond, and Recover to strengthen organizational security.

NIST Incident Response Lifecycle: Guides incident handling through preparation, detection, containment, eradication, recovery, and lessons learned.

Diamond Model: Correlates adversaries, infrastructure, capabilities, and victims during investigations.

Pyramid of Pain: Emphasizes detecting attacker TTPs over easily changed indicators like IP addresses and hashes.

Key Takeaways

Improved understanding of widely used cyber defence frameworks.

Learned how SOC analysts map alerts to attacker behavior.

Gained insight into structured incident response and threat detection strategies.

Developed knowledge of security governance and defensive operations.

